# Branches merged into fork-integration, in order.
#
# One git ref or owner:branch per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
# Use `origin/<name>` for branches you push; a bare name means a local branch.
# Use `owner:branch` for someone else's github.com/owner/paseo branch. Each
# update fetches the author's tip, including force-pushes; we never rebase it.
#
# `fork/integrate.sh add <branch>` appends a line here and merges the branch
# in; a line added by hand is merged by the next `fork/integrate.sh rebase`.
# Removing a line takes effect at the next `fork/integrate.sh rebuild`, which
# is also the only time the order matters: for conflict resolution, the branch
# you want to "win" goes last.
#
# fork-base is not listed: it is the branch this file lives on, and it is
# always merged first.
#
# When a PR lands upstream, delete its line and rebuild. The commits arrive
# through upstream/main instead.

